  "title": "Erdős Problem #563",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $F(n,\\alpha)$ denote the smallest $m$ such that there exists a $2$-colouring of the edges of $K_n$ so that every $X\\subseteq [n]$ with $\\lvert X\\rvert\\geq m$ contains more than $\\alpha \\binom{\\lvert X\\rvert}{2}$ many edges of each colour.\nProve that, for every $0\\leq \\alpha< 1/2$, $ F(n,\\alpha)\\sim c_\\alpha\\log n $ for some constant $c_\\alpha$ depending only on $\\alpha$.",
